message: If you use MOSAIC, please cite the software using the metadata below.
type: software
title: 'MOSAIC: Mission-Oriented Self-Organization through Auctions, Incentives, and Coalitions'
version: 0.4.0
date-released: '2026-07-30'
authors:
- family-names: Molina
  given-names: Katherin
  affiliation: Independent Researcher, Australia
- family-names: Holguin
  given-names: Lorena
  affiliation: Kahlo Group
abstract: MOSAIC is an agent-based NetLogo model of decentralized mission coordination among
  heterogeneous robots through local sensing, dynamic communication, auctions, incentives,
  reputation, adaptive strategies, and temporary coalition formation.
keywords:
- agent-based modeling
- NetLogo
- multi-robot systems
- multi-agent systems
- decentralized coordination
- coalition formation
- task allocation
- complex systems
- BehaviorSpace
